  "composer": "Traditional",
  "about": "This carol began as a dance tune called Branle de l'Official. It was printed in 1589 in Orchésographie, a dance book by the French cleric Thoinot Arbeau. The English composer George Ratcliffe Woodward wrote the carol's words, and it was published in 1924. Charles Wood harmonised it.",
  "funFact": "Thoinot Arbeau was a pen name. The man behind it was Jehan Tabourot.",
